.TH HYPOT 3
.SH NAME
hypot, cabs \- Euclidean distance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <math.h>

double
hypot(x, y)
double x, y;

double
cabs(z)
struct { double x, y; } z;
.fi
.PP
cc ... \-lm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hypot
returns
.PP
.nf
	sqrt(x * x + y * y)
.fi
.PP
the length of the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose other sides are
.I x
and
.IR y ,
and the distance of the point
.RI ( x ", " y )
from the origin. It takes care not to overflow, or to lose precision,
when the squares would be too large or too small for a double: the
result is within half a unit in the last place.
.PP
.B cabs
returns the same for a complex number, a structure of its real and
imaginary parts.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
When the result is too large, HUGE.
.SH ERRORS
errno is set to ERANGE when the result is too large.
.SH SEE ALSO
sqrt(3), matherr(3), intro(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B hypot
function first appeared in Version 2 AT&T UNIX, and
.B cabs
in Version 7.
